TESTSUITE "NESTBND nested boundaries"

*> All three boundary statements live inside conditional bodies: a CALL
*> in an IF branch, a CALL in an EVALUATE WHEN branch, and an EXEC SQL
*> inside an IF -- the layouts the nested-mock-targets design makes
*> spliceable.
TESTCASE "nested call, when-branch call, nested sql all fire"
    MOCK CALL "DISCRATE"
        MOVE 5 TO WS-DISC-RATE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK CALL "TAXCALC"
        MOVE 7 TO WS-TAX-RATE
    END-MOCK
    MOCK SQL "UPDATE ORDERS"
        MOVE 0 TO SQLCODE
    END-MOCK
    PERFORM MAIN-PROCESS
    EXPECT WS-DISC-RATE TO BE 5
    EXPECT WS-TAX-RATE TO BE 7
    EXPECT WS-SQL-STATUS TO BE "OK"
    VERIFY CALL "DISCRATE" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY CALL "TAXCALC" WAS CALLED ONCE
    VERIFY SQL "UPDATE ORDERS" WAS PERFORMED ONCE
